Cilium L7 policy enforcement extends network security beyond IPs and ports. Using eBPF and Envoy, Cilium can inspect application-layer traffic such as HTTP, gRPC, Kafka, and DNS. Policies can allow or deny specific URLs, HTTP methods, headers, or API calls. Combined with Cilium identities derived from Kubernetes labels, security policies remain consistent even when pod IPs change, providing zero-trust microsegmentation for Kubernetes workloads.
